//! Automatic differentiation for f64 code on core's `Array`.
//!
//! Forward mode carries derivatives alongside values: `Dual` (one
//! direction), `Duals<N>` (N directions per evaluation), `HyperDual`
//! (exact second derivatives) and `Jet` (Taylor series of any order).
//! Reverse mode records a `Tape` of `Var` operations and sweeps it back
//! once, so the gradient of f: R^n -> R costs a small multiple of one
//! evaluation whatever n is. A function written once over `Smooth` runs
//! in every mode. `grad`, `jacobian`, `hessian`, `jvp`, `vjp` and
//! `derivatives` pick the mode from the number type the function takes.
//!
//! `∂` and `∇` (feature `ops`) return a derivative in the form of what
//! they are given, never a value at a point: a function for a function,
//! samples for samples; the value is `∂(f)(x)`. They dispatch through
//! the `Derive` and `Gradient` traits, so other packages extend the same
//! two names. Every result is exact to rounding: no step sizes.
//!
//! Pure Nabi: every target, wasm included, gets the same results.

#[cfg(feature = "ops")]
pub mod ops;

mod diff;
mod dual;
mod grid;
mod hyper;
mod jet;
mod lanes;
mod smooth;
mod tape;

pub use diff::{ScalarFn, VectorFn, derivative, derivatives, grad, hessian, jacobian, jvp, seed, value_grad, value_jacobian, vjp};
pub use dual::Dual;
pub use hyper::HyperDual;
pub use jet::Jet;
pub use lanes::Duals;
pub use smooth::Smooth;
pub use tape::{Adjoints, Tape, Var};
